2. License grant

Subject to the conditions below, the Licensor grants you a worldwide,
non-exclusive license, without a license fee, to install, run, copy, build, and
modify the Software for either of these purposes:

  (a) Personal Use; or
  (b) the internal operations of a Company Group whose total Headcount is
      strictly fewer than 250 people.

You may also redistribute the Software as provided in section 5. These
permissions cover the Licensor's copyright and any patent claims controlled by
the Licensor that are necessarily infringed by the permitted use of the Software.

3. Specific limitations on use without a paid license

"Personal Use" means use by an individual solely for that individual's private,
non-business purposes. Use for an employer, client, or other organization is
organizational use, even on a personally owned device or through a personal
account, and must meet the Company Group limit or be covered by a paid license.

"Company Group" means the company or other organization for whose benefit the
Software is used, together with all entities that directly or indirectly control
it, are controlled by it, or are under common control with it. This includes
parent companies, subsidiaries, and sister companies. An organization includes
a sole proprietorship, partnership, corporation, association, nonprofit,
educational institution, or government body. "Control" means ownership of more
than half of the voting rights or the power to direct management and business
policies, whether through ownership, agreement, or another arrangement.

"Headcount" means the total number of distinct individuals working as employees
or individual contractors anywhere in the Company Group. Include contractors
supplied through staffing agencies or personal service companies while they
work for the group. Count full-time and part-time workers as one person each,
regardless of their role, location, working hours, or whether they use ShareFrame.
Count each person only once across the group; do not count only the team,
department, subsidiary, or people using the Software.

There is no revenue limit. Revenue, funding, and valuation do not affect
eligibility. A Company Group with 249 people qualifies; one with 250 or more
does not. Organizational use is assessed against the benefiting Company Group,
including when the individual operating the Software is an external contractor.
If a use benefits multiple Company Groups, each must qualify for free use or
that use must be covered by a paid commercial license.
There is no separate exemption for educational, nonprofit, or government use.

Eligibility must continue throughout use. If growth, an acquisition, a change
of employer or client, or another change makes the use ineligible, obtain a paid
license before continuing that use. You may resume free use if it subsequently
meets these conditions again. Personal Use remains free regardless of the size
of the individual's employer, provided it is genuinely independent of that work.

4. Paid commercial licensing

Any use outside section 2, including organizational use by a Company Group with
250 or more people, requires a separate paid commercial license agreed with the
Licensor before that use begins or continues. Copying, building, or modifying
the Software for such organizational use does not avoid this requirement.

The commercial agreement specifies its fees, permitted users, duration, and any
support or other commitments. No price, subscription, automatic charge, or
support entitlement is created by this public license. If you do not obtain the
required commercial license, you must refrain from the otherwise unlicensed use.
Where a signed commercial agreement expressly replaces these terms, that
agreement governs the use it covers.

For commercial licensing, contact the maintainer through:
https://github.com/apetersson/qnd/issues

